摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Refreshable Cloudflare quick-tunnel pool for the dsh web GUI — phone access with QR + embedded login","id":"gh:1343656184","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"phone-tunnel-pool","slug":"iimaguest/phone-tunnel-pool","topics":["cloudflare","dsh","dsh-plugin","quick-tunnel","web-gui"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Refreshable Cloudflare quick-tunnel pool for the dsh web GUI — phone access with QR + embedded login"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# phone-tunnel-pool — Cloudflare quick-tunnel pool for the dsh web GUI"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Enable/disable a **self-healing Cloudflare quick-tunnel pool** for\n`http://127.0.0.1:3080` (the Deep"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"Seek Harness web GUI) from a floating widget\nwith a scannable QR code. One scan from your phone, and"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" the pool keeps\nitself alive:"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- **Generational rotation (12h):** a new pair of tunnels spawns on schedule;\nolder generations stay "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"alive while anything is still on them.\n- **Chase service worker:** every origin your browser touches"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" registers a\nservice worker. Dead or rotated hostnames redirect to a live sibling or the\nnewest prim"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ary — the same open tab survives generation changes as long as\nit stays connected.\n- **Prompt-free m"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"igrations:** the proxy injects credentials only into pages it\nhas already authenticated; before any "},{"id":"p5s6","text":"redirect the watchdog pre-authenticates\nthe target hostname (minting its auth cookie), so migrations"},{"id":"p5s7","text":" land\nauthenticated — no \"Authentication required\" popups.\n- **Usage-based retirement:** generations"},{"id":"p5s8","text":" retire only when idle\n(no tabs / websockets / recent traffic) or at a hard age cap.\n- **Respawn wit"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"h backoff:** dead tunnels are replaced with new hostnames;\nquick-tunnel mint quota (Cloudflare 429) "},{"id":"p5s10","text":"is respected via exponential\nbackoff + a 2-probe dead-grace (DNS propagation)."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Extra: the daemon runs detached and **adopts** across `dsh web` restarts, so\nthe same URL, password "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"and QR stay valid until you click Disable — no\nre-scan (an OS reboot still costs one fresh scan; a n"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"amed tunnel removes even\nthat — see `PLAN.md` §7)."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Install / Uninstall"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"After install: open the widget → **Enable** → scan the QR with your phone\ncamera. Install/remove rec"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"oncile `dsh.profile.bundles` against the installed\nstate automatically — **never edit `~/.dsh/profil"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"es/web/package.json` by hand**;\na stray bundle entry with no matching dependency is exactly the kind"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" of state\nthat fails profile boot (\"cannot resolve profile bundle\")."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Prerequisites (all of them)"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| What | Needed? | Who provides it |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| `dsh web` running on its default port **3080** (`DSH_TARGET_PORT` to override) | required | you (t"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"he plugin tunnels *to* it) |\n| `cloudflared` binary on PATH | required | you — `brew install cloudfl"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"ared` (or apt/dnf/Chocolatey, or set `DSH_CLOUDFLARED` to the existing binary) |\n| Node.js runtime |"},{"id":"p12s4","text":" required | dsh itself — no separate install (the daemon reuses dsh's node) |\n| `python3` + `qrcode`"},{"id":"p12s5","text":" package | optional | you — `pip install qrcode`; without it the widget shows URL + login instead of"},{"id":"p12s6","text":" a scannable QR |\n| `caffeinate` | optional | macOS ships it; skipped elsewhere |\n| PowerShell | opt"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"ional | Windows ships it — used only for process cleanup on Windows (no `pkill` there) |\n| Outbound "},{"id":"p12s8","text":"network | required | cloudflared → Cloudflare edge on 443/7844 (no inbound port needed) |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The widget **preflights these on dsh web start** and shows a yellow warning\nline (with the exact fix"},{"id":"p13s2","text":", e.g. `brew install cloudflared`) before you even\nclick Enable; the daemon also fails fast with a r"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"eadable error if cloudflared\nis missing at Enable time, and `refresh` in the popup re-checks everyth"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"ing —\na stale error clears once the prereqs pass."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The feature flag set is version-gated on `cloudflared --version`:\n2024.6+ enables the opt-in post-qu"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"antum handshake (`DSH_PQ=1`), 2024.8+ adds\n`--management-diagnostics=false`; older builds (apt/dnf p"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ackages) get a\nreduced, compatible flag set."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**Platforms.** macOS, Linux and Windows (Windows uses PowerShell for process\ncleanup; `caffeinate` i"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"s macOS-only and silently skipped elsewhere). The\ndaemon's state file and log live in the per-OS tem"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"p directory\n(`os.tmpdir()`); the widget settings file (`iptunnel-settings.json`) lives in\n`~/.dsh`."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### The dsh 0.2 launch token (why the tunnel 401'd)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"dsh 0.2 moved web auth into the connection service: the desktop URL carries a\nper-process launch tok"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"en (`http://127.0.0.1:3080/?token=<secret>`), a valid\ntoken exchange mints a signed browser-session "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"cookie, and every request with\nneither gets `401`. The tunnel path is phone → trycloudflare → this p"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"roxy →\nthe GUI, and a phone can never learn a token that only exists in the desktop\nprocess output —"},{"id":"p17s5","text":" so on 0.2 the tunnel answered 401 all the way down."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The fix (0.3.35): the plugin reads the token through the connection service's\npublic `authenticatedU"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"rl()` API and hands it to the proxy — via the daemon\nenvironment on a fresh enable, and via `POST /i"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ptunnel/__ctl/launch-token`\nwhenever a surviving daemon outlives a dsh restart (the token is\nper-pro"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"cess, the daemon is deliberately not). The proxy exchanges the token\nagainst the GUI once, holds the"},{"id":"p18s5","text":" resulting session cookie, and stamps it onto\nevery forwarded request and websocket handshake — re-m"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"inting on an upstream\n401 and on every token push. A phone therefore presents only this proxy's\nBasi"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"c auth, exactly as before, and the launch token never reaches cloudflared's\nenvironment, the QR, or "},{"id":"p18s8","text":"the published URL. On a dsh without the gate the token\nis empty, every new code path no-ops, and for"},{"id":"p18s9","text":"warding is byte-identical to the\npre-0.2 behaviour (`test/launch-token.test.mjs` pins all of this ag"},{"id":"p18s10","text":"ainst a\nmock origin, including rotation)."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Security model"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"- The password is **generated per Enable**, held in memory, shown in the\nwidget and embedded in the "},{"id":"p20s2","text":"QR; nothing is committed or published. (The\ndaemon keeps the *current* credentials in a `0600` state"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" file under the OS\ntemp dir so the tunnel survives a dsh web restart; that file is deleted on\ndisabl"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"e.)\n- `/iptunnel/*` service paths (health, sw-config, sw.js, entry, watchdog.js,\ntelemetry, preauth)"},{"id":"p20s5","text":" are **public by necessity** — browsers fetch service\nworkers without credentials; they carry hostna"},{"id":"p20s6","text":"mes and pool liveness only.\nThe credential handoff (`/iptunnel/preauth`) mints a cookie only for a\nc"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"aller presenting the valid password; it never echoes anything.\n- `window.__ptAuth` is injected **onl"},{"id":"p20s8","text":"y into HTML the proxy has authenticated**.\n- The proxy listens on 127.0.0.1; public network exposure"},{"id":"p20s9","text":" happens only\nthrough the tunnel hostnames — **the QR/hostname is a bearer secret**\n(anyone who gets"},{"id":"p20s10","text":" it can open the tunnel while enabled): disable when done.\n- Quick tunnels are testing-grade (no upt"},{"id":"p20s11","text":"ime SLA, per-IP mint quota).\nThe repo-agnostic sibling package\ncarries the same pattern for any loca"},{"id":"p20s12","text":"l port; a named tunnel is the\nlifetime endgame (one stable hostname → no re-scans, no prompts, no qu"},{"id":"p20s13","text":"t; a named tunnel is the\nlifetime endgame (one stable hostname → no re-scans, no prompts, no quota)."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
